        ":question/problem": "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{(x+3)y}\n$$\n\nWork on an open domain where all displayed expressions are defined and the dependent-variable factor is nonzero. Choose an equivalent equation in the form $A(y)\\, \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=B(x)$, with a multiplier depending only on $y$ and a right-hand side depending only on $x$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Expose the independent-variable and dependent-variable factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{(x+3)y}=\\frac{x}{x+3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by the reciprocal of the dependent-variable factor. On the stated domain, this gives\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative multiplier depends only on $y$ and the right-hand side only on $x$.",
